# CONTRIBUTING

If you are reading this it means that you are probably interested in contributing to the language.
I am glad!

## How to contribute?

Feel free to create issues and discussions.

Contributions must be made through a comprehensive pull request to the `dev` branch.

## Coding conventions

Please follow the rules defined by the formatter and linters in use.

## Testing

- `cargo test` runs everything: in-tree unit tests plus `tests/e2e.rs`, which
  compiles every `samples/*.fib` through the library API and executes the
  result (exact-stdout asserts for the deterministic samples, `fib_bench`
  compile-only). It needs the default `llvm` feature and a C compiler.
- `cargo test --lib` runs only unit tests (also works with
  `--no-default-features`); `cargo test --test e2e` runs only the
  end-to-end suite.
- Conventions for new code:
  - Every new lowering branch ships with a `samples/*.fib` reproducer so e2e
    covers it.
  - Every soundness fix ships with a `get_typed_err` negative test.
  - For diagnostics, assert on `is_err()` plus a message substring/line —
    not the exact full message, which is still evolving.
